  - Slate text (`#1c1d21`) with lighter muted tones (`#575a65`).
  - Signature Blue accents (`#334ab3`) for primary actions, avoiding heavy gradients or neon.
- **Structure:** Split layouts (content left / visual right), overlapping floating elements, clear distinct feature sections.

## Voice & Tone
- **Human, not corporate:** Write like a person explaining a tool to a friend. No "synergize," "leverage," or "seamless."
- **Direct & Honest:** State what the checked-out app does and which parts require a Mac. Do not turn planned work into a feature claim. Maintain the "source-only / unverified" notes but format them elegantly so they don't break the polished feel.
- **Quiet Confidence:** Explain the benefit without hype, forced jokes, profanity, emojis, or exclamation marks.

## Composition Notes
- The hero is split: Strong, oversized serif headline driving the value proposition, paired with clear CTAs.
- The transparent float mode is the hero capability—celebrate it visually.
- Do NOT fabricate features or copy Sketch's product claims.

## Copy examples

| Prefer | Avoid |
| --- | --- |
| “Pause for the question. Pick up where you left off.” | “Unlock seamless presentation excellence.” |
| “Float your notes right over the meeting.” | A generic headline that hides compact transparent mode |
| “Build from source. Prebuilt installation is not available yet.” | “Download now” when no verified download exists |
| “Your scripts stay on this device. Make a backup before clearing its data.” | “Your work is always safe.” |
